# Azure VM & Supabase Migration Plan

We are shifting the focus to setting up the Azure VM and migrating the staging database to **Supabase**. This will improve stability and offload heavy 2GB+ SQL processing from your VM.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Supabase Connection**: You will need to provide your Supabase **Connection String** (Transaction mode). It should look like `postgresql://postgres.[ID]:[PASSWORD]@aws-0-us-west-1.pooler.supabase.com:6543/postgres`.

> [!CAUTION]
> **VM Security**: The VM currently only has port 22 (SSH) open. Once we deploy the app, you will need to open **ports 8000 (API)** and **3000 (Web)** in the Azure portal (Networking/NSG settings).

## Proposed Changes

### 1. Supabase Migration

#### [MODIFY] [docker-compose.yml](file:///home/eisen/Downloads/SQAuto/docker/docker-compose.yml)
- Comment out or remove the local `postgres` and `redis` services (if you want to use Supabase for DB and potentially Azure/Redis later, though local Redis is fine for now).
- Update the `api` and `worker` to depend directly on the external Supabase URL.

#### [MODIFY] [.env.example](file:///home/eisen/Downloads/SQAuto/.env.example)
- Update with Supabase-specific placeholders.

### 2. Azure VM Setup Script

#### [NEW] [setup_vm.sh](file:///home/eisen/Downloads/SQAuto/scripts/setup_vm.sh)
Create a script to run on the VM that:
- Installs Docker and Docker Compose.
- Sets up the firewall to allow API and Web traffic.
- Configures the `.env` file from secrets.

### 3. CI/CD for VM

#### [NEW] [deploy.yml](file:///home/eisen/Downloads/SQAuto/.github/workflows/deploy.yml)
- Automated build and push to Docker Hub.
- SSH deployment to the new Azure VM.

